      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لَهُ الرَّجُلُ لَهُ الْوَلَدُ أَ يَسَعُهُ أَنْ يَجْعَلَ مَالَهُ لِقَرَابَتِهِ فَقَالَ هُوَ مَالُهُ يَصْنَعُ بِهِ مَا شَاءَ إِلَى أَنْ يَأْتِيَهُ الْمَوْتُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Abdullah Bin Al Mubarak, from Abdullah Bin Jabala, from Sama’at, from Abu Baseer, ",
          "(The narrator says) ‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘The man has the son for him, does he have the leeway to make his wealth to be for his relatives?’ So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is his wealth. He can place it wherever he so wishes to until the death comes upon him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Hassan from ‘Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak from ‘Abd Allah ibn Jabalah from Sama‘ah from abu Basir who has narrated the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who has a son; if he can give his assets to his relatives. He (the Imam) said, ‘They are his assets, he can do to it whatever he wants until death comes upon him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
